  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a string SSS. Find the number of ways to choose an unordered pair of non-overlapping non-empty substrings of this string (let's denote them by s1s_1s1​ and s2s_2s2​ in such a way that s2s_2s2​ starts after s1s_1s1​ ends) such that their concatenation s1+s2s_1 + s_2s1​+s2​ is a palindrome.\n\nTwo pairs (s1,s2)(s_1, s_2)(s1​,s2​) and (s1′,s2′)(s_1', s_2')(s1′​,s2′​) are different if s1s_1s1​ is chosen at a different position from s1′s_1's1′​ or s2s_2s2​ is chosen at a different position from s2′s_2's2′​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤∣S∣≤1,0001 \\le |S| \\le 1,0001≤∣S∣≤1,000",
      "SSS contains only lowercase English letters",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (25 points):** ∣S∣≤100|S| \\le 100∣S∣≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first and only line of the input contains a single string SSS.",
    "outputFormat": "Print a single line containing one integer — the number of ways to choose a valid pair of substrings.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "abba",
        "output": "7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe following pairs of substrings can be chosen: (\"a\", \"a\"), (\"a\", \"ba\"), (\"a\", \"bba\"), (\"ab\", \"a\"), (\"ab\", \"ba\"), (\"abb\", \"a\"), (\"b\", \"b\")."
      }
    ]
  },
